{%- doc -%}
  Loads the recently viewed component's script.

  Rendered by any section holding a `<ui-recently-viewed>`. Rendering it more than
  once on a page is harmless — a module runs once however many tags point at it,
  which is the same bargain [ui-carousel] makes.

  The element itself is markup the section writes, and it needs three things: the
  search route to ask, its own section id to ask for, and the product being looked
  at so that page is recorded and kept out of its own row.

  @example
  <ui-recently-viewed
    id="row-{{ section.id }}"
    data-url="{{ routes.search_url }}"
    data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    data-limit="5"
    hidden
  >
    …a row of product cards, each `<li>` carrying `data-product-id`…
  </ui-recently-viewed>
  {% render 'ui-recently-viewed' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

<script src="{{ 'ui-recently-viewed.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>
